.²1 The foot (whether of men or animals); {#tayorjagfhatuH pAdAn#} <ls>R. 1. 57</ls>;
 {#pAdayornipatya, pAdapatita#} <ab>&c.</ab> (The word {#pAda#} at the end of
 comp). is changed to {#pAd#} after {#su#} and numerals; {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} {#supAd#},
 {#dvipAd, tripAd#} <ab>&c.</ab>; and also when the first member is used as a standard
 of comparison, but is a word other than {#hasti#} <ab>&c.</ab>; see <ls>P. V. 4. 138-140</ls>;
 {%<ab>e. g.</ab>%} {#vyAGrapAd#}. The <ab>nom.</ab> <ab>pl.</ab> of {#pAda#} is often added to names
 of persons or titles of address to show great respect or veneration; {#mfzyantu#}
 {#lavasya bAliSatAM tAtapAdAH#} <ls>U. 6</ls>; {#jIvatsu tAtapAdezu#} <ls n="U.">1. 19</ls>; {#devapAdAnAM#}
 {#nAsmABiH prayojanam#} <ls>Pt. 1</ls>; so {#evamArADyapAdA AjYApayanti#} <ls>Prab. 1</ls>;
 so {#kumArilapAdAH#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 A ray of light; {#bAlasyApi rabeH pAdAH patantyupari BUBftAm#} <ls>Pt. 1. 328</ls>;
 <ls>Śi. 9. 34</ls>; <ls>R. 16. 53</ls> (where the word has sense 1 also).
.²3 The foot or leg of an inanimate object, as of a bed-stead; {#catuzpadI#}
 {#hi niHSreRI brahmaRyeva pratizWitA#} <ls>Mb. 12. 20. 4</ls>.
.²4 The foot or root of a tree; as in {#pAdapa#}.
.²5 The foot of a mountain, a hill at the foot of a mountain ({#pAdAH pratyantaparvatAH#});
 {#revAM drakzyasyupalavizame vinDyapAde viSIrRAm#} <ls>Me. 19</ls>; <ls>Ś. 6. 17</ls>.
.²6 A quarter, fourth part; as in {#sapAdo rUpakaH#} ‘one and one fourth
 rupee’; <ls>Ms. 8. 241</ls>; <ls>Y. 2. 174</ls>; {#kArzApaRe dIyamAne pAdo'pi datto Bavati#}
 <ls>ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 20</ls>.
.²7 The fourth part of a stanza, a line.
.²8 The fourth part of a chapter or book, as of the Adhyāyas of Pāṇini,
 or of the Brahma-sūtras.
.²9 A part in general.
.²10 A column, pillar; {#sahasrapAdaM prAsAdaM … aDirohanmayA dfzwaH#}
 <ls>Mb. 5. 143. 30</ls>.
.²11 A foot as a measure equal to twelve Aṅgulis.
.²12 The quadrant of a circle.
.²13 The foot-hole or bottom of a water-skin; {#indriyARAM tu sarvezAM#}
 {#yadyekaM kzaratIndriyam . tenAsya kzarati prajYA dfteH pAdAdivodakam ..#} <ls>Ms. 2. 99</ls>.
.²14 A wheel; {#girikUbarapAdAkzaM SuBaveRu triveRumat#} <ls>Mb. 3. 175. 4</ls>; <ls>Ki. 12. 21</ls>.
.²15 A golden coin (weighing one tola); {#sa ha gavAM sahasramavaruroDa#}
 {#daSa daSa pAdA ekEkasyAH SfNgayorAbadDA baBuvuH#} <ls>Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 1</ls>.

